        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-4 text-justify">
          <a href="https://icpc.global/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The <strong>International Collegiate Programming Contest (ICPC)</strong></a>
          is the largest computer programming contest in the world. The ICPC provides college students with an opportunity to
          demonstrate and sharpen their problem-solving and computing skills, and is often regarded as the
          <em>&ldquo;Olympics of Computer Programming.&rdquo;</em>
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-4 text-justify">
          The <strong>ICPC Asia Regional Contests</strong> invite Asian students to meet, establish friendships, and promote fair competition in programming.
          The <strong>ICPC Asia Regional Contest, Kanpur Site</strong> extends the same spirit of collaboration and excellence.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold mt-6 sm:mt-8 mb-2 sm:mb-3">A Little About Us</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed text-justify">
          ICPC is a two-tier contest. The world is divided into six regions, and <strong>Asia</strong> is one of them.
          In Asia, there are many regional sites and <strong>Kanpur</strong> is one of these sites. Each regional site selects one
          winning team that becomes eligible to participate in the World Finals. The Kanpur Site contest will be held at
          <strong>CSJM University, Kanpur</strong>. Due to limited seats in the Kanpur Site Regional Round, a preliminary online
          contest is organized to select teams for the regional round. The Kanpur Site regional round will be held on
          <strong>22–23 December 2025</strong>. This contest is hosted by the
          <strong><a class="underline" href="https://csjmu.ac.in/school-of-engineering-and-technology/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">School of Engineering and Technology (formerly UIET)</a>, <a class="underline" href="https://csjmu.ac.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CSJM University, Kanpur</a></strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
